### [EFFECT-08] count-up
Used in: SECTION-03 (both stat cards, both hero variants), SECTION-06 (three manifesto figures)

`lib/hooks.ts`, `useCountUp`:

```ts
export function useCountUp(to: number, run: boolean, reduce: boolean, duration = 1600) {
  const [value, setValue] = useState(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!run) return;
    if (reduce) {
      setValue(to);
      return;
    }
    let raf = 0;
    const start = performance.now();
    const tick = (now: number) => {
      const t = Math.min(1, (now - start) / duration);
      const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - t, 3);
      setValue(Math.round(to * eased));
      if (t < 1) raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    };
    raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    return () => cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
  }, [run, to, reduce, duration]);

  return value;
}
```

Cubic ease-out (`1 - (1-t)^3`) driven by a raw `requestAnimationFrame` loop, not a Framer `animate()` call. `run` is always sourced from a `useInView(ref, { once: true, margin: "..." })` -- do **not** add a "has it already run" ref guard inside the hook itself: in React Strict Mode the effect mounts, cleans up and remounts once, and a same-hook guard would let the second mount bail out before the counter starts, freezing it at zero. The `once: true` on the caller's `useInView` is what already guarantees a single run. Call sites: `useCountUp(150, inView, reduce, 1500)` (classes stat, desktop `1500`/mobile `1400`ms), `useCountUp(10, inView, reduce, 1500)` (members stat), `useCountUp(value, inView, reduce, 1400)` per Manifesto figure (`12`, `3`, `40`).

