**Every string quoted in the tables below is a `HERO` key, not a literal** (SETUP-CONTENT): `"Pr"` = `HERO.brandParts.pr`, `"Gravi"` = `HERO.brandParts.gravi`, `"ty"` = `HERO.brandParts.ty`, the two tagline lines = `HERO.tagline[0]` and `HERO.tagline[1]` (two fragments each), the paragraph = `HERO.body`, the two buttons = `HERO.buttons`, the two stat cards = `HERO.stats`, and the `sr-only` headline = `HERO.srTitle`. `HeroDesktop` and `HeroMobile` both read the same keys -- a string written twice is a bug.

The coordinates themselves never move into `content.ts`. **Coordinates are design; strings and URLs are content.** That split is what keeps this hero pixel-faithful and still editable.

Layer 1 -- backdrop, outside the frame, full-bleed on the section root. It is **not written inline**: it is the two-layer recipe declared in `BACKGROUNDS.hero` (SETUP-CONTENT), rendered by the one component that owns every background in this build (SETUP-BACKDROP):

